From 8fff5055884a2f7ef0fc1087bd658336b19c11d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 12:29:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 235/257] fix(execution): reconcile U2a declaration fields
 against their ground truth

The U2a verifier's recomputed-digest forgery probe showed 10 declaration
fields were accepted and executed (artifact.kind/library/pack, selected
library fingerprint, numeric guarantee class/deterministic/reduction order,
fallback.primary, request.policy_digest, thread mode).

- add pypto.execution.binding_verify: content-local reconciliation of policy
  digest, selected/numeric/artifact/fallback declarations against the frozen
  policy/selected/contract/rule documents, plus report cross-block checks
- ExecutionPlan.validate now refuses all content-local declaration forgeries
- entry._execute always re-runs the deterministic resolver for the frozen
  policy against the digest-checked capability snapshot (caller-supplied or
  synthesized from the default local provider probe) and refuses any payload
  difference before provider invocation; unregistered providers keep their
  PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE reason
- validate_report_schema refuses single-field report forgeries for artifact
  kind/library/pack, fallback primary/used, guarantees numeric class and the
  policy digest; manifest-only double-forgeries are explicitly registered as
  report-layer boundaries (execution re-resolution still refuses them)
- tests: convert the U2a probe's 9 accepted fields plus the thread-mode case
  into must-reject/exempted regressions, cover double-forgery and report
  single-field forgeries
